<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix21: The Dead Man's Switch x Combat Extended - startup errors:
         CE ammo injector found no recipe named MakeAmmo_155mmHowitzerShell_Anti
         CE ammo injector found no recipe named MakeUSH_Shell_ADP
         (and the same for MakeShell_AntigrainWarhead when it appears)

       ROOT CAUSE: DMS's bundled CE patch (3121742525, 1.6/CE/Patches/AmmoProduction.xml) adds
       CE_AutoEnableCrafting_DMS_TableAmmoPrinter to the tradeTags of CE's ABSTRACT ammo bases so
       its ammo printer can craft everything. Its xpath names AmmoBase, MediumAmmoBase and
       HeavyAmmoBase, but only AmmoBase actually has a tradeTags node, so the tag lands there -
       the root of every CE ammo def. RimWorld merges inherited list nodes, so every ammo def
       inherits the tag, and CE's AmmoInjector (AmmoInjector.cs, "Toggle craftability") then
       demands a RecipeDef named Make<defName> for each. Three defs in this modlist are
       deliberately recipe-less, so each logs a red error at every startup:

         Ammo_155mmHowitzerShell_Anti  - CE core, antigrain 155mm (loot/trade only by design)
         Shell_AntigrainWarhead        - CE core, antigrain 81mm  (same)
         USH_Shell_ADP                 - Ushankas Glittertech Expansion; CE's own ModPatches
                                         compat rewrites it into an AmmoDef under
                                         81mmMortarShellBase, no recipe

       Same failure class as upstream CE issue #4408 (DMS + other victim mods). DMS's patch even
       contains a commented-out Inherit=False guard for Shell_AntigrainWarhead - the author found
       this exact problem, then disabled the guard.

       FIX: set Inherit="False" on each def's tradeTags so the DMS tag never reaches it, then
       re-add AmmoBase's legitimate tags verbatim (CE_AmmoInjector marks the def for AmmoInjector
       processing, CE_Ammo puts it in ammo trader stock - dropping those would break trading).
       Each def's own tags (CE_AutoEnableTrade_Sellable on the two CE shells) survive Inherit=False
       untouched. Net effect: identical to the pre-DMS resolved tags. These three simply stay
       un-craftable at the DMS ammo printer, which is vanilla-CE behaviour.

       Deliberately NOT fixed by stripping the DMS tag from AmmoBase itself - that would disable
       DMS's ammo-printer crafting for every ammo type in the game, which is its intended feature.

       Both mods must be active; FindMod wrappers are NESTED because a multi-entry <mods> list is
       OR, not AND (see Fix20). USH_Shell_ADP gets a third FindMod for its source mod.

       success is NOT Always: the FindMod gates make this inert when a mod is absent, so an inner
       failure can only mean CE renamed these defs or their tradeTags shape changed (master has
       already split the ammo bases once) - hear about it rather than let it rot (Fix14 lesson). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Combat Extended</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
      <mods>
        <li>The Dead Man's Switch</li>
      </mods>
      <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
        <operations>

          <li Class="PatchOperationAttributeSet">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Ammo_155mmHowitzerShell_Anti"]/tradeTags</xpath>
            <attribute>Inherit</attribute>
            <value>False</value>
          </li>
          <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Ammo_155mmHowitzerShell_Anti"]/tradeTags</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>CE_AmmoInjector</li>
              <li>CE_Ammo</li>
            </value>
          </li>

          <li Class="PatchOperationAttributeSet">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Shell_AntigrainWarhead"]/tradeTags</xpath>
            <attribute>Inherit</attribute>
            <value>False</value>
          </li>
          <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Shell_AntigrainWarhead"]/tradeTags</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>CE_AmmoInjector</li>
              <li>CE_Ammo</li>
            </value>
          </li>

          <!-- The AmmoDef that CE's ModPatches substitutes in has no tradeTags element at all,
               so the whole element is added, inheritance-blocked, with AmmoBase's tags. -->
          <li Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
            <mods>
              <li>Ushankas Glittertech Expansion</li>
            </mods>
            <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
              <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="USH_Shell_ADP"]</xpath>
              <value>
                <tradeTags Inherit="False">
                  <li>CE_AmmoInjector</li>
                  <li>CE_Ammo</li>
                </tradeTags>
              </value>
            </match>
          </li>

        </operations>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
